From: Alex Lennon <ajlennon@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: st1010: fix HX8279-D multi-drop vertical timing

The module timing table lists a 1944-line total but also lists porch and sync
values which add up to 1951 lines.  The HX8279-D controller specification
clarifies the multi-drop timing convention: for 1200x1920 the 1944-line total
uses a 14-line vertical front porch and a 10-line back interval which includes
the 2-line sync pulse.

Express that timing in DRM terms as 14 front, 2 sync and 8 back.  This keeps
the specified 156 MHz pixel clock and 1944-line total while giving the master
and slave HX8279-D controllers their documented synchronization intervals.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-himax8279d.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-himax8279d.c
@@ -1159,8 +1159,8 @@ static const struct drm_display_mode santek_st1010_display_mode = {
 	.hsync_end = 1200 + 60 + 24,
 	.htotal = 1340,
 	.vdisplay = 1920,
-	.vsync_start = 1920 + 17,
-	.vsync_end = 1920 + 17 + 2,
+	.vsync_start = 1920 + 14,
+	.vsync_end = 1920 + 14 + 2,
 	.vtotal = 1944,
 };
